{"t_ms": 862343, "conversation_id": "v2llm_streaming_retrieve_s037", "turn_id": 1, "actor": "system", "event_type": "retrieval_result", "payload": {"passages": ["# corpus/ \u2014 Hotel Documents\n\n**Owner: Lakshya**\n\n## What this folder is\n\nThe hotel's documents live here: the knowledge the assistant answers from. About 60 short \ndocuments covering things like pool and gym hours, check-in and check-out rules, menus, and \npolicies.\n\n## How to fill it\n\nSee the full instructions in `retrieval/README.md` (Step 1). In short:\n- Write ~60 short documents, one topic per file, as `.txt` or `.md`.\n- Make them realistic and varied.\n- Deliberately plant a few contradictions (e.g. one doc says the pool closes at 10 PM, \n  another says 9 PM) and keep a note of which ones, for a later experiment.\n\nThe index-building script reads every file in this folder, so anything you put here becomes \npart of the searchable knowledge.\n", "In-room Safe Instructions\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nEvery room is equipped with an electronic safety locker for storing valuables such as passports, cash, jewelry, and electronic devices. Guests are advised to set a personal PIN while using the safe. The hotel is not responsible for valuables left unsecured outside the in-room safe. For additional assistance, guests may contact the Front Desk.", "Printing & Photocopy Services\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nPrinting, scanning, and photocopying services are available through the Business Centre. Guests may email their documents to the Business Centre or use the available workstations. Standard printing charges apply, while basic scanning services are provided free of charge for registered hotel guests."], "scores": [0.8649169206619263, 0.9920817017555237, 1.0542290210723877], "filenames": ["README.md", "20_room_safe.txt", "46_printing_services.txt"], "timing_policy": "sentence_end", "timing_trigger": "sentence_end", "user_end_known_at_finish": true, "launch_offset_ms_vs_user_end": 100, "overlap_with_speech_ms": 0, "forecast_invalidated": false}}
